Stop everything for now. But there's a problem: both your verification and your plan are wrong. If something can clearly be handled by rules, then of course use rules — but I think that makes the game feel rigid. Sure, some things probably are just rules, so we need to look into how other people do it: which parts use rules, which use decision trees, and which use upper-layer AI. The "rules" you're talking about feel like scripts to me. It's not that they can't be used — it's about which layer they go in and when to use what. Get this straight first, and define the problem clearly first. This may need to be confirmed against the skill system and the other systems first.
